/-!
# A functor fixing the zero-dimensional coherent sheaves is fully faithful

This file proves the criterion [Stacks, Tag 0G25] for full faithfulness by `Ext` between
closed-point skyscrapers, and then [Stacks, Tag 0G26].

Let `k` be a field, `X` a proper regular scheme over `k` and `F : D_perf(𝒪_X) ⥤ D_perf(𝒪_X)` a
`k`-linear exact functor with `F(𝓕) ≅ 𝓕` for every coherent `𝓕` with `dim Supp(𝓕) = 0`. Then
`F` is fully faithful: this is [Stacks, Tag 0G26].

## The proof

By [Stacks, Tag 0G25] it suffices that `F` induces bijections
`Ext^i(𝒪_x, 𝒪_{x'}) ⟶ Ext^i(F(𝒪_x), F(𝒪_{x'}))` for closed points `x, x'`. Source and target are
isomorphic finite-dimensional `k`-vector spaces ([Stacks, Tag 0FYC]), so injectivity or
surjectivity suffices.

* For `x ≠ x'` both sides vanish: `Hom(𝒪_x, 𝒪_{x'}[i]) = Hom((𝒪_x)_{x'}, κ(x')[i])` by the
  stalk-skyscraper adjunction, and the stalk of `𝒪_x` at `x' ≠ x` is zero.
* For `i < 0` both sides vanish (t-structure).
* For `i = 0`, every nonzero endomorphism of `𝒪_x` is an isomorphism (the derived skyscraper is
  fully faithful and `κ(x)` is a simple `𝒪_{X,x}`-module), so `F` is injective on it.
* For `i = 1`, complete `ξ : 𝒪_x ⟶ 𝒪_x[1]` to a distinguished triangle
  `𝒪_x ⟶ B ⟶ 𝒪_x ⟶ 𝒪_x[1]`. Then `B` is a coherent sheaf in degree zero supported at `x`, so
  `F(B) ≅ B`. In a distinguished triangle `T` with finite-dimensional Hom spaces,
  `T.mor₃ = 0` if and only if `dim Hom(T₃, T₂) = dim Hom(T₃, T₁) + dim Hom(T₃, T₃)`; as the
  objects of `F(T)` are isomorphic to those of `T`, `F(ξ) = 0` forces `ξ = 0`.
* For `i > 1`, `Ext^*(𝒪_x, 𝒪_x) = Ext^*_{𝒪_{X,x}}(κ, κ)` (the derived skyscraper is fully
  faithful) is generated by `Ext¹` because `𝒪_{X,x}` is a regular local ring
  (`IsRegularLocalRing.closure_range_ext_comp_residueField_eq_top`, the local content of
  [Stacks, Tag 0BQY]); so surjectivity in degree one gives surjectivity in every positive degree.

## Main results

* `bijective_map_shift_perfectPointSheaf_of_fixes_zeroDimensional`: the Ext maps between
  closed-point skyscrapers are bijective.
* `fullyFaithful_iff_bijective_ext_perfectPointSheaf`: [Stacks, Tag 0G25].
* `fullyFaithful_of_fixes_zeroDimensional`: [Stacks, Tag 0G26].

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G26](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G26)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G25](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G25)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

